{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788113690679331275,"compiled_state":{"alias":"bleareyed-claimable-quelea","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"bd22c974740568d091fcf7d7742bcfb506c872737ee94e8a346ea497774d89be","event_uuid":"7e3736f3-4506-49cc-86b8-caa6b4f60319","position":{"commit_sha":"75739bf44a6aaf4c69f82f980b4fab6e03dea609","position":"1788109253593886326-7e3736f3-4506-49cc-86b8-caa6b4f60319"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"aea07a5b845938b67e36a8fd7ef50a9ebabebd24331e1843df69a25a53f4a871","event_uuid":"aa70cd46-ad39-469f-8a32-fd232c9be630","position":{"commit_sha":"b6346e6de470a9abd7b40c9d3354055884b745d5","position":"1788109307095655521-aa70cd46-ad39-469f-8a32-fd232c9be630"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"13621699176ed8346088848b8bce6fab48b2d029dae79f5561b89bcd0ac0a0ab","event_uuid":"ca83007d-4883-412f-a097-bc8702df1010","position":{"commit_sha":"9d77374bd4f7a88da01fc5cee48f4029f2ff0bb2","position":"1788109307098546212-ca83007d-4883-412f-a097-bc8702df1010"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788109253593886326,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"aa70cd46-ad39-469f-8a32-fd232c9be630","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"73d8-4871-1b49-4047"},{"link_uuid":"ca83007d-4883-412f-a097-bc8702df1010","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"551b-1a30-ac2b-4127"}],"description":"Spun from 73d8 (brainy-convulsant-unicorn) and 551b (sanidine-cilium-eland) during the 2026-08-30 error-code decision pass.\n\n## Problem\n`error_code_for` (`src/rebar/_errors.py`) branch 6 maps ANY `LLMError → llm_unavailable`. That over-claims an AI-provider outage for many faults that are not outages — every non-availability `LLMError`/`WorkflowError` subclass (editor missing-bundle, workflow parse/wiring, etc.). This is the residual of origin 8a31's blanket mapping and the systematic completion of epic 3405's descriptiveness intent.\n\n## Fix\nNarrow branch 6 so `llm_unavailable` fires ONLY for `LLMUnavailableError` (the true transient-outage type). Every other `LLMError` subclass falls through to its explicit `error_code` attribute (branch 5) if it has one, else to `command_failed` (branch 7) — honest \"unclassified\", not a false outage.\n\n## Blast radius (must sweep)\nEnumerate ALL `LLMError` subclasses (`src/rebar/llm/errors.py` + workflow error classes). For each, confirm the post-change code is correct: a genuine transient outage must remain `LLMUnavailableError → llm_unavailable`; anything else must land on an accurate code. Add held-out tests through real surfaces proving (a) an execute-time outage still returns `llm_unavailable`, (b) a non-outage `WorkflowError` (e.g. the editor missing-bundle at `editor.py:475`) returns `command_failed`.\n\n## Resolves 551b\nThis delivers 551b's ruling: editor missing-bundle → `command_failed`, no new vocabulary. The finer `environment_unready` code for a missing local build artifact stays DEFERRED (revisit trigger: `edit_workflow` becoming classifier-reachable on a live MCP surface); analysis retained on 551b.\n\n## Coordination\nTouches `src/rebar/llm/` = eb64 (financial-stoneware-brant) DECLARED SCOPE. Implement in coordination with eb64. `_errors.py` itself is top-level (not eb64).\n\n## Acceptance\n- [ ] branch 6 narrowed to `LLMUnavailableError`; all other `LLMError` subclasses sweep-verified to accurate codes.\n- [ ] Held-out tests: outage → `llm_unavailable`; editor missing-bundle → `command_failed`; through real surfaces.\n- [ ] caused_by 8a31 recorded at close.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["error-codes","llm","eb64-coord"],"ticket_id":"ce6b-cffa-6450-4fa5","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Reserve llm_unavailable for true outages: narrow error_code_for branch 6 to LLMUnavailableError","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["7e3736f3-4506-49cc-86b8-caa6b4f60319","aa70cd46-ad39-469f-8a32-fd232c9be630","ca83007d-4883-412f-a097-bc8702df1010"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788113690679331275,"uuid":"eafb5ec7-0266-4745-846b-9e9bae82ea4e"}